TinyX
=====

TinyX is an embeddable X11 server core derived from the traditional
DIX/MI/FB/KDrive server architecture. It provides:

- a static C library with a small host-facing API in `include/tinyx.h`;
- a memory-backed depth-24/32-bpp framebuffer with Damage reporting;
- descriptor-free X11 client byte streams;
- cooperative, bounded server stepping;
- pointer and keyboard injection;
- runtime resize, host-controlled DPI, and configurable X11 visuals;
- built-in filesystem-free bitmap text and cursor fonts;
- native static-library and Emscripten module targets;
- headless C and TermX terminal reference embedders.

Build
-----

    cmake -S . -B build/native -G Ninja
    cmake --build build/native
    ctest --test-dir build/native --output-on-failure

The build requires X.Org protocol headers. See `docs/build.md` for dependency
overrides, installation, and Emscripten instructions, and `embedders/README.md`
for the host model and reference embedders.

Scope
-----

The supported product is the embeddable memory-display server. Hardware and
legacy native-host sources inherited from the original TinyX tree remain for
reference but are not built.

Licensing
---------

The TinyX library and TinyX-specific core changes are GPL-3.0-only. The sample
embedders are available under either MIT or GPL-3.0-only; executables linked
with TinyX remain subject to GPL-3.0-only. See `LICENSE.md`, `COPYING`, and
individual source-file notices.
